  "id": "COMPOUND:33280 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "Sarcotrine A appears to have a target relationship with BT-474 through a series of molecular interactions, with Hepatocyte and Raji being intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Sarcotrine A may act on Hepatocyte, which in turn targets Licochalcone D, and this pathway leads to BT-474. Similarly, Sarcotrine A may also target Raji, which is targeted by Maplexin A, ultimately leading to BT-474. These findings indicate that Sarcotrine A may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the activation of downstream targets that ultimately influence BT-474. The integration of these pathways suggests that Sarcotrine A may act as a modulator of cellular processes that are relevant to BT-474, potentially through the activation of specific signaling pathways or metabolic pathways. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism where Sarcotrine A influences cellular targets that are functionally linked to BT-474, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
